The contract test verifies that the `Remove` method of the `ArrayList` class correctly removes an instance of the specified element from the list.

In the test method `PUT_RemoveContract`, we assume a scenario where we have an `ArrayList` object `arrList` and an element `x` that exists in `arrList`. Before removing the element, we store the initial state of the `arrList`, its count, and the index positions of `x` in the list.

After removing `x` from `arrList`, we store the new state of `arrList`, and then compare the old and new states to observe the behavior of the `Remove` method.

Additionally, we use `Assert` to verify that the count of `arrList` has decreased by 1, and that the index of `x` has been changed to -1 in the new state.

The `Assert.AreNotEqual` assertion checks that the count of `arrList` before and after removing `x` differs.

The assertion `Assert.AreEqual(-1, arrList.IndexOf(x))` verifies that the index of `x` has been changed to -1 after removing it.

The assertion `Assert.AreNotSame(Old_arrListIndexOfX, New_arrListIndexOfX)` ensures that the index of `x` in the new state is different from its old index.

The assertion `Assert.IsFalse(arrList.Contains(x))` asserts that `x` is not present in the `arrList` after removing it.

Overall, by observing the initial and new states, we can verify that the `Remove` method correctly removes an element from the list and updates the index and count accordingly.

This approach ensures that the `Remove` method behaves as expected and meets the specified contract for the ArrayList class.--------------------            Assert.AreNotEqual(Old_arrListCount, Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ array list contains x is not true in old array  
            Assert.IsTrue(!Old_arrListContainsX); 

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ array list count equals to new array list count -1
            Assert.AreEqual(New_arrListCount, Old_arrListCount - 1);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ array list contains x is not true in new array  
            Assert.IsTrue(!New_arrListContainsX); 

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ array list index of x equals to last index of x in new array  
            Assert.AreEqual(New_arrListIndexOfX, New_arrListLastIndexOfX);

            Assert.AreEqual(New_arrListIndexOfX, -1);
        }

