[Updated] I got two more assertions that you can use. Here is the revised code: 

```csharp
// Act
old_index = list.IndexOf(item);  // Index of the item before removal
list.Remove(item);
new_index = list.IndexOf(item);  // Index of the item after removal

// Assert
// Check if the item was removed by verifying its absence from the ArrayList
Assert.IsTrue(old_index != -1 && new_index == -1);
```

This assertion checks if the Index of the item before it gets removed is -1 (which means it does not exist in the ArrayList) and after it gets removed it is also -1, thus confirming the item is effectively removed from the ArrayList. 

```csharp
// Assert
// Check the count reduction after removal
Assert.AreEqual(old_Count - 1, list.Count);
```

